WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:13.400
- Begin irradiation.
- Sir.

2
00:00:24.633 --> 00:00:25.833
Oh, my.

3
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.700
Your power, it's truly terrifying, my little Z2.

4
00:00:29.866 --> 00:00:32.066
Such an incredible thing to see.

5
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.533
Huh?

6
00:00:49.066 --> 00:00:50.733
You seem sad, Squishy.

7
00:00:53.766 --> 00:00:57.900
♪ Squishy, Squishy You're, oh, so very soft ♪

8
00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:01.800
♪ Squishy, Squishy You're, oh, so pretty green ♪

9
00:01:01.933 --> 00:01:05.800
♪ Squishy, Squishy The cutest I've ever seen ♪

10
00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:09.366
♪ You're happy sleeping in My bag, Squishy ♪

11
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.133
- Bonnie, something wrong?
- Nothing.

12
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.266
Wow! Hey, look, they're exhibiting a beautiful gem at the hotel.

13
00:01:21.933 --> 00:01:23.033
I wanna see.

14
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:25.366
- Beautiful gem?
- Pika?

15
00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:27.766
- We should all go.
- You really want to?

16
00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:29.000
- Sure do.
- Sure do.

17
00:01:29.766 --> 00:01:31.766
Uh, then why don't we go check it out?

18
00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:33.266
- Can't wait.
- Can't wait.

19
00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:40.366
Our heroes are on their way

20
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.366
to Serena's Master Class Showcase in Gloire City.

21
00:01:43.433 --> 00:01:45.966
But for now they're visiting Jacore Town.

22
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.366
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

23
00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:04.300
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

24
00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:08.199
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

25
00:02:08.266 --> 00:02:10.866
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

26
00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:12.433
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

27
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.766
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

28
00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:19.000
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

29
00:02:19.066 --> 00:02:20.733
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

30
00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.000
It's already closed for the day?

31
00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:37.466
Yes, I'm afraid it is. Come back another time, please.

32
00:02:37.533 --> 00:02:39.866
I was really looking forward to it.

33
00:02:39.933 --> 00:02:43.500
- I know. Do you have an available room?
- Why, yes, we do.

34
00:02:44.066 --> 00:02:47.866
Let's stay here tonight, and go see the exhibit first thing in the morning.

35
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.500
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

36
00:02:58.733 --> 00:03:00.766
I'm only after one thing.

37
00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.000
Let's go to bed early tonight for tomorrow.

38
00:03:11.066 --> 00:03:11.900
Mm-hm!

39
00:03:13.666 --> 00:03:14.500
Pika!

40
00:03:14.566 --> 00:03:16.133
- What's that?
- So loud.

41
00:03:16.866 --> 00:03:18.133
It sounds like an alarm.

42
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.500
- It's the top floor.
- The gem exhibit.

43
00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.466
Did they say gem exhibit?

44
00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.800
Wonder what's wrong.

45
00:03:23.866 --> 00:03:25.333
Hey, let's go check it out.

46
00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.700
The diamond is still here.

47
00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.966
Looks like nothing was stolen.

48
00:03:32.933 --> 00:03:35.733
That's strange. All they did was open the lock.

49
00:03:40.466 --> 00:03:41.300
Who are you?

50
00:03:42.066 --> 00:03:43.766
Master Thief Keyes.

51
00:03:43.966 --> 00:03:45.433
Who opened the lock?

52
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:46.666
Why, I did.

53
00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.933
Ha-ha-ha! Well, then, good night.

54
00:03:55.533 --> 00:03:57.600
- Come back.
- Contact Officer Jenny.

55
00:03:58.533 --> 00:04:00.200
Master Thief Keyes?

56
00:04:01.633 --> 00:04:04.100
Yes, this is definitely his handiwork.

57
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.066
You were watching, too. Tell me exactly what you saw.

58
00:04:08.733 --> 00:04:12.366
He threw that card, then escaped through that window.

59
00:04:12.533 --> 00:04:16.300
He laughed and called himself Master Thief Keyes.

60
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.266
I'm sorry I'm late.

61
00:04:20.833 --> 00:04:22.633
Is this where it took place?

62
00:04:23.466 --> 00:04:26.233
Yes. I'm sorry I had to call you in.

63
00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.066
- Let's see.
- Here.

64
00:04:30.266 --> 00:04:33.633
Yes, that's mine. There's no doubt that I made this lock.

65
00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:34.800
No way.

66
00:04:34.866 --> 00:04:36.600
You made that lock yourself?

67
00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:38.933
Ed is a locksmith.

68
00:04:40.566 --> 00:04:43.333
My name's Ash and this is my partner, Pikachu.

69
00:04:43.533 --> 00:04:44.633
I'm Serena.

70
00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.533
My name's Bonnie and that's Dedenne up there.

71
00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:49.900
And this is Squishy.

72
00:04:49.966 --> 00:04:50.866
I'm Clemont.

73
00:04:51.066 --> 00:04:53.033
It's really not that impressive.

74
00:04:54.333 --> 00:04:56.566
After all, he managed to unlock it.

75
00:04:56.666 --> 00:05:00.766
See, for some strange reason, every one of Master Thief Keyes' incidents

76
00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:04.166
- have been targeting Ed's locks.
- Wow, that sounds so weird.

77
00:05:04.233 --> 00:05:05.400
I wonder why.

78
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.900
I'd say that he might be holding a grudge against Ed.

79
00:05:19.766 --> 00:05:23.766
- It's music to my ears.
- Let's get that lug to join Team Rocket.

80
00:05:23.833 --> 00:05:28.300
That way we'll be able to pick any kind of lock that needs picking. Handy.

81
00:05:28.733 --> 00:05:31.433
- We'll break in anywhere, any day.
- Yay!

82
00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.633
- This is all so weird.
- Who'd have thought we'd witness

83
00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:40.900
- an incident like this?
- They're calling off the gem exhibit, too.

84
00:05:40.966 --> 00:05:42.966
All because of that Master Thief.

85
00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:46.666
What I'd like to find out is who that guy really is.

86
00:05:53.433 --> 00:05:55.266
- What is that?
- Agh!

87
00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:57.600
- Get it off, get it off.
- Bonnie, no.

88
00:05:57.666 --> 00:05:58.600
Take it easy.

89
00:06:00.833 --> 00:06:03.033
- It's stuck.
- Hold on, I'll help.

90
00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.566
- That hurts.
- That hurts.

91
00:06:15.533 --> 00:06:16.366
Stop.

92
00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.400
Get off of my head.

93
00:06:21.633 --> 00:06:24.633
Sounds like it's trying to tell us something.

94
00:06:25.733 --> 00:06:27.966
Binacle, the two-handed Pokémon.

95
00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.166
Binacle live in pairs, two on the same rock.

96
00:06:31.366 --> 00:06:34.000
If they fight, one of them finds a new rock.

97
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.433
The PokéDex says there should be another one.

98
00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.133
It's true that Binacle always come in pairs.

99
00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.533
So, what does it mean?

100
00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:46.466
Maybe it has something to do with the way this Binacle is sticking to Bonnie's head.

101
00:06:47.233 --> 00:06:48.600
Wow, you think so?

102
00:06:48.866 --> 00:06:50.166
Is that you, Righty?

103
00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:57.900
- Oh, what?
- Excuse me, is this your Pokémon?

104
00:06:58.066 --> 00:07:00.766
Yes. We had a fight a while back.

105
00:07:01.066 --> 00:07:04.766
And it's been missing ever since. Righty, where have you been?

106
00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:08.166
I told you to forget about Lefty.

107
00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:11.300
Now, you get off of this little girl. Let's go.

108
00:07:13.233 --> 00:07:16.600
You are so stubborn! Who taught you to act that way?!

109
00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.166
- Wouldn't it be a good idea to calm down?
- She's right.

110
00:07:20.233 --> 00:07:25.033
- Why did you two get into a fight?
- Maybe we can figure out what happened.

111
00:07:25.666 --> 00:07:27.166
All right, all right.

112
00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:31.600
Righty has been looking around everywhere trying to find Locke.

113
00:07:37.366 --> 00:07:38.400
No, that's wrong.

114
00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.200
Slow it down.

115
00:07:40.366 --> 00:07:43.500
That's no way to handle that poor lock. Stop.

116
00:07:43.566 --> 00:07:44.466
But sir...

117
00:07:45.266 --> 00:07:46.333
Give it to me.

118
00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:51.066
I'll have to tell you again. People and locks are much the same.

119
00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:56.133
When you're trying to get someone to open up, you treat them with kindness.

120
00:07:57.633 --> 00:08:00.200
You still have a lot of learning to do.

121
00:08:03.433 --> 00:08:06.400
My apprentice left shortly after that incident...

122
00:08:07.266 --> 00:08:09.466
along with the other Binacle, Lefty.

123
00:08:09.566 --> 00:08:12.700
- Then what?
- Righty really wanted to find them both.

124
00:08:12.766 --> 00:08:16.866
So, I said, "Do whatever you want. I have no time for the likes of them."

125
00:08:16.933 --> 00:08:20.800
Once those two had made the decision to leave me, then I was through.

126
00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:23.866
Oh, then that explains why Righty is still mad.

127
00:08:24.366 --> 00:08:26.100
Yeah. It sure does.

128
00:08:26.866 --> 00:08:29.300
Righty, will you stop causing all this trouble?

129
00:08:29.366 --> 00:08:31.466
Get off of that little girl, now!

130
00:08:32.966 --> 00:08:33.799
You--

131
00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.033
Wait. Please calm down.

132
00:08:36.466 --> 00:08:39.933
Perhaps it would be a good idea if Righty stays with us tonight.

133
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.766
- Mm-hm, mm-hm.
- Huh?

134
00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:42.766
Stays with you?

135
00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.033
I'll take good care of Righty.

136
00:08:48.233 --> 00:08:50.366
Okay, but just for tonight.

137
00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.633
You'd better not cause any trouble.

138
00:08:53.333 --> 00:08:57.233
Now that that's all settled, let's go and look for Lefty and Locke tomorrow.

139
00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.766
Yeah!

140
00:09:08.066 --> 00:09:10.700
I've got such a troublesome apprentice.

141
00:09:11.366 --> 00:09:13.433
Only we could unlock this.

142
00:09:14.333 --> 00:09:17.700
My difficult apprentice and myself.

143
00:09:21.633 --> 00:09:25.433
Once he sees how I opened that lock, he'll have to admit how good I am.

144
00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:26.833
He'll just have to.

145
00:09:28.833 --> 00:09:32.700
You're right. We're a team. I owe you a lot for helping so much.

146
00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:39.966
Binacle number two dead ahead. The lug it's with

147
00:09:40.033 --> 00:09:43.200
- must be that Master Thief Keyes.
- So, catch that duo.

148
00:09:43.666 --> 00:09:44.766
We're off.

149
00:09:49.633 --> 00:09:51.000
What's going on here?

150
00:09:52.366 --> 00:09:55.966
- You're Master Thief Keyes, aren't you?
- And who are you?

151
00:09:56.033 --> 00:09:59.933
If you want the gem, I don't have it. I would never steal anything.

152
00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:02.033
That's of no concern to us.

153
00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.633
Our real business is with you and your partner, Binacle.

154
00:10:05.866 --> 00:10:06.966
Binacle?

155
00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:15.466
All right, let's find Ed's apprentice and Lefty right now.

156
00:10:15.533 --> 00:10:16.366
Pika!

157
00:10:16.433 --> 00:10:18.866
First, we just have to figure where to start.

158
00:10:18.933 --> 00:10:20.833
It would help to have a clue.

159
00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.333
Ha, ha. This is where I come in.

160
00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.566
Because the future is now. Thanks to science.

161
00:10:26.633 --> 00:10:28.566
Clemontic Gear on.

162
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.566
I thought we'd encounter a situation precisely like this one.

163
00:10:32.633 --> 00:10:34.766
This is my Binacle Finder.

164
00:10:34.833 --> 00:10:36.566
You and your boring invention names.

165
00:10:36.633 --> 00:10:39.600
It's actually not a Binacle-specific finder,

166
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.533
- but let's call it that for now.
- Lazy, too.

167
00:10:43.133 --> 00:10:44.733
We can find it with that?

168
00:10:44.966 --> 00:10:48.233
Yes. Binacle live in pairs, so, all we need to do

169
00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:51.433
is find a Pokémon with the same exact biometric data

170
00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.566
as this Binacle.

171
00:10:54.066 --> 00:10:55.266
Power, on.

172
00:10:57.166 --> 00:10:58.433
We're ready to go.

173
00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:01.366
Wow, science is so amazing.

174
00:11:02.066 --> 00:11:03.100
Huh?

175
00:11:03.733 --> 00:11:04.666
I found it.

176
00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:07.700
- It's that way.
- We'll find your buddy in no time.

177
00:11:12.666 --> 00:11:14.666
Who's that Pokémon?

178
00:11:19.066 --> 00:11:21.366
It's Binacle.

179
00:11:28.033 --> 00:11:31.066
- What's this?
- The back of the Pokémon Center.

180
00:11:31.266 --> 00:11:33.166
We're going to open up the storage house,

181
00:11:33.233 --> 00:11:36.166
and make off with every single Pokémon inside.

182
00:11:36.766 --> 00:11:38.566
Right up your alley, palley.

183
00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.966
Picking that should be a breeze.

184
00:11:42.333 --> 00:11:43.766
All right. I'll do it.

185
00:11:47.733 --> 00:11:51.333
But first, undo this restraint. How can I use my hands?

186
00:11:51.766 --> 00:11:54.600
- He does have a point.
- Set him free, old chum.

187
00:11:54.666 --> 00:11:55.500
Righty-o.

188
00:11:58.033 --> 00:11:59.466
Let's go, Lefty.

189
00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:02.233
Chop-chop.

190
00:12:03.366 --> 00:12:05.033
A pile of Pokémon awaits.

191
00:12:05.533 --> 00:12:07.533
Yeah. Or maybe not.

192
00:12:08.133 --> 00:12:09.500
I don't steal!

193
00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:11.366
Lefty, Brick Break.

194
00:12:14.566 --> 00:12:16.566
- Hey, Meowth.
- Let's go. Quick.

195
00:12:17.566 --> 00:12:22.233
Hey, you two aren't getting away. Quick, Gourgeist, front and center, now!

196
00:12:23.766 --> 00:12:25.133
Inkay, you too!

197
00:12:27.833 --> 00:12:28.833
Seed Bomb.

198
00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:29.733
Use Psybeam!

199
00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.500
Don't I know you?

200
00:12:38.566 --> 00:12:39.866
Nurse Joy, help.

201
00:12:39.933 --> 00:12:43.933
Get Officer Jenny. They're trying to steal every Pokémon you have.

202
00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.833
- Use Psybeam!
- Use Seed Bomb!

203
00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.133
Huh?

204
00:12:59.166 --> 00:13:01.200
We're blasting off again!

205
00:13:15.566 --> 00:13:18.300
- Huh? Oh, no.
- A fire.

206
00:13:19.633 --> 00:13:20.933
It says this is it.

207
00:13:21.166 --> 00:13:22.966
- No way.
- Let's hurry.

208
00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.700
- Oh, no.
- It's dangerous.

209
00:13:26.133 --> 00:13:29.666
But there are so many Pokémon inside. They need our help.

210
00:13:32.933 --> 00:13:33.766
I know.

211
00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:36.066
Nurse Joy?

212
00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:41.733
Righty?

213
00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.266
- Locke, you work for Ed.
- Yeah.

214
00:13:44.466 --> 00:13:47.033
Righty has been looking for you and Lefty.

215
00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:48.800
Looking for us?

216
00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.566
Not now. First things first.

217
00:13:51.666 --> 00:13:54.800
- We need to put out the fire right away.
- I know.

218
00:13:55.033 --> 00:13:56.233
Do you have the key?

219
00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:57.666
We need it right now.

220
00:13:57.733 --> 00:14:00.466
I must have dropped it during the explosion.

221
00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.900
- Okay. Then contact the Fire Department.
- Right.

222
00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:05.866
Now what?

223
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.166
There are Pokémon inside. My partner and I know what to do.

224
00:14:11.166 --> 00:14:12.866
We'll simply save them all.

225
00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.333
Let's go, Lefty.

226
00:14:15.733 --> 00:14:16.866
- But wait.
- Pika!

227
00:14:19.666 --> 00:14:22.866
- Look out!
- All right, we need to put out that fire.

228
00:14:23.466 --> 00:14:25.466
Greninja, use Water Shuriken.

229
00:14:30.133 --> 00:14:31.566
- Here.
- You can do it.

230
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.833
Righty, can you use Water Gun?

231
00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.033
Do it, now!

232
00:14:43.233 --> 00:14:44.766
Okay, now is your chance.

233
00:14:48.566 --> 00:14:51.766
All right, Lefty, it's time. Do it like we always do.

234
00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.300
Unh! Keep it coming.

235
00:14:59.733 --> 00:15:02.133
Righty, keep using Water Gun.

236
00:15:16.366 --> 00:15:17.200
We did it.

237
00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:24.566
Now, Lefty, let's put all of the PokéBalls here in this cart.

238
00:15:39.566 --> 00:15:41.800
Unh! It's stuck.

239
00:15:42.533 --> 00:15:44.233
Can you hear me? Anyone?

240
00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.900
- Yeah.
- The door won't open.

241
00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:47.933
What?

242
00:15:50.766 --> 00:15:52.600
What are we gonna do now?

243
00:15:52.833 --> 00:15:54.500
I'm not really sure.

244
00:15:57.066 --> 00:15:59.500
- Where are you going?
- Gotta go get help!

245
00:16:04.133 --> 00:16:05.866
There are Pokémon inside.

246
00:16:05.933 --> 00:16:06.800
Got it.

247
00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.866
What's that? Huh?

248
00:16:11.933 --> 00:16:13.033
Help, please.

249
00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:14.633
That girl. It's you.

250
00:16:18.166 --> 00:16:19.600
What's going on?

251
00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.433
Is everyone okay?

252
00:16:33.166 --> 00:16:34.200
Bonnie, Ed.

253
00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:37.833
Of course. You went with Righty to go and get Ed.

254
00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:40.166
All right. The entry door won't open.

255
00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:41.533
She told me.

256
00:16:41.966 --> 00:16:43.366
Now, work time, Righty.

257
00:16:44.566 --> 00:16:45.400
Wait.

258
00:16:45.866 --> 00:16:47.700
It's dangerous. Stay back.

259
00:16:47.766 --> 00:16:50.333
I have to go save my apprentice.

260
00:16:51.433 --> 00:16:52.366
Hey, wait.

261
00:16:57.033 --> 00:16:59.066
Hey, it's me. Are you all right?

262
00:17:00.233 --> 00:17:01.066
It's Ed.

263
00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:05.466
A locksmith never ever gives up when trying to open a lock.

264
00:17:05.666 --> 00:17:09.599
I taught you to always try to open every lock, didn't I?

265
00:17:09.933 --> 00:17:12.433
- Ed.
- Your hands stuck together?

266
00:17:13.933 --> 00:17:17.366
I was just giving myself a little break. Lefty, let's go.

267
00:17:18.333 --> 00:17:19.400
That's the spirit.

268
00:17:19.466 --> 00:17:23.066
I'll work on it from the outside, so you work on it from the inside.

269
00:17:23.133 --> 00:17:25.099
- Okay.
- See the rotary latch?

270
00:17:25.266 --> 00:17:26.099
I do.

271
00:17:26.166 --> 00:17:29.633
It's a difficult job. There are five of them inside.

272
00:17:30.133 --> 00:17:34.600
Move the back latch to the right twice, move the closest latch to the left once

273
00:17:34.666 --> 00:17:37.566
and then the middle latch over to the right by one.

274
00:17:37.633 --> 00:17:41.066
I'll hold on to any damaged parts. Give me a hand, Righty.

275
00:17:42.433 --> 00:17:45.033
Good. Quickly. We're running out of time.

276
00:17:45.433 --> 00:17:47.766
Right. Lefty, I'm counting on you.

277
00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:55.166
Now, compose yourself and stay calm.

278
00:17:56.666 --> 00:17:59.166
Gently. Gently.

279
00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:12.533
Please, Ed, there's something I wanna tell you in case this doesn't work.

280
00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:15.800
Be quiet and move those hands!

281
00:18:16.233 --> 00:18:19.233
Master Thief Keyes, who's been opening your locks,

282
00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:20.266
that guy's me.

283
00:18:20.566 --> 00:18:23.033
I wanted you to acknowledge my skills.

284
00:18:23.566 --> 00:18:24.600
I knew that.

285
00:18:25.833 --> 00:18:29.500
Do I have to spell everything out for you? There are only two people

286
00:18:29.566 --> 00:18:32.800
who have the skill to open those locks, me and you.

287
00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:36.700
Yes, you're already a fine locksmith.

288
00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:39.833
You mean it?

289
00:18:50.466 --> 00:18:53.166
Listen, this is where it all counts the most.

290
00:18:53.266 --> 00:18:54.533
All right, sir.

291
00:19:09.366 --> 00:19:11.133
Well done, my apprentice.

292
00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:12.033
Thanks.

293
00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:13.366
We did well, didn't we?

294
00:19:21.433 --> 00:19:24.066
Wow, so, you're Master Thief Keyes, huh?

295
00:19:24.133 --> 00:19:26.100
And you knew the whole time?

296
00:19:26.166 --> 00:19:27.000
Yes.

297
00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:30.366
I'm sorry for all the trouble I caused you. Really.

298
00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.366
You have to pay the price for what you did.

299
00:19:33.966 --> 00:19:34.800
I know.

300
00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:40.966
Lefty. Thanks, pal.

301
00:19:42.266 --> 00:19:45.466
So, you can tell me all about it down at the station.

302
00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.833
I hope you'll come back when you're a free man.

303
00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:51.100
I'll leave the door unlocked. Count on it.

304
00:19:53.266 --> 00:19:54.100
Thank you, Ed.

305
00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.533
Glad things turned out okay.

306
00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:05.166
He'll always have a place to come back to.

307
00:20:05.233 --> 00:20:08.900
With all his talent, there's no doubt he's a great locksmith.

308
00:20:08.966 --> 00:20:11.966
Hey, kids, this stays between us, all right?

309
00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:15.233
Since all Locke did was open locks,

310
00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:19.033
I'll go ahead and issue him a warning and he'll be released in no time at all.

311
00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:20.666
Sorry for all of this.

312
00:20:22.266 --> 00:20:25.833
- Really?
- I figured by keeping quiet for a change,

313
00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.500
I could teach him a lesson.

314
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.433
After witnessing the bond

315
00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.800
between a skilled master and his apprentice,

316
00:20:34.866 --> 00:20:37.700
along with the bond between people and Pokémon,

317
00:20:37.833 --> 00:20:42.200
our heroes once again realize the importance of a trusting relationship

318
00:20:42.633 --> 00:20:44.800
as the journey continues.
